# HSL (Hue, Saturation, Luminance)

HSL allows adjustment of specific colors in an image by controlling hue (color shift), saturation (intensity), and luminance (brightness) for individual color channels.

## Common Uses

- **Skin tones**: Adjust oranges to look natural
- **Blue sky**: Increase saturation for dramatic sky
- **Green foliage**: Adjust to look natural

Related to [[Post-Processing]] and [[Global vs Local Adjustments]].
